Wow, usually my knights suck but now Robbie the Knight is really
working it! The pony died pretty quickly but I got another one who
became a warhorse. Then I polymorphed him into a baby gray dragon and
soon he was a mighty dragon killing all the shop keepers, priests
(after I had bought some protection of course) and pretty much
everything else in the dungeon.

I had reflection, BoH and Excalibur but I was concerned about not
having MR... Then a cunning plan bumped into my mind! What if my gray
dragon dies and he leaves scales and I then bring him back to life with
my wand of undead turning?.. Sounded brilliant but the problem was he
wasn't going to die because he killed everything and ate everything.
And I didn't have the heart to lock him in a room and wait for him to
starve. So I just had to stick with my mithril coat.

Then I went to the Quest. I have to admit that I was going to face
Ixoth without MR and AC at -11. I didn' t know whether Ixoth used some
nasty spells or not but I guess I would have died if I had proceeded.
Yes, Hoss II died and left scales. How nice of him! He just hadn't
learned that acidic monsters (such as ochre jellies) are _dangerous_.
And then I revived him and he was still my friend although I had taken
his scales. :) Guess he has spare scales and he doesn't mind.

Ixoth was tougher than I had thought. But: What the heck is the tile
image of him?!? Why does he look like a balrog? I thought he would look
like all the other dragons in Nethack. He is a dragon, right? I just
don't get it.

One question: Does the Magic Mirror of Merlin shatter if I kick it? Or
is it unbreakable?

